  "question": {
    "text": "If the system of equations\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& x+2 y-3 z=2 \\\\\n& 2 x+\\lambda y+5 z=5 \\\\\n& 14 x+3 y+\\mu z=33\n\\end{aligned}$\nhas infinitely many solutions, then $\\lambda+\\mu$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "13",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "10",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "12",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "11",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Delta=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n1 & 2 & -3 \\\\\n2 & \\lambda & 5 \\\\\n14 & 3 & \\mu\n\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\Rightarrow \\lambda \\mu+42 \\lambda-4 \\mu+107=0 \\\\\n& \\Delta_1=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n2 & 2 & -3 \\\\\n5 & \\lambda & 5 \\\\\n33 & 3 & \\mu\n\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\Rightarrow 2 \\lambda \\mu+99 \\lambda-10 \\mu+255=0 \\\\\n& \\Delta_2=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n1 & 2 & -3 \\\\\n2 & 5 & 5 \\\\\n14 & 33 & \\mu\n\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\Rightarrow \\mu=13\n\\end{aligned}$\nAlso, $\\lambda=-1$\nHence, $\\lambda+\\mu=13-1=12$"
  }
